==English==
{{was wotd|2018|January|2}}

===Etymology===
[[File:CumulonimbusFlorida.jpg|thumb|[[cumulonimbus|Cumulonimbus]] [[cloud#Noun|clouds]] forming over the [[Gulf of Mexico]], seen from [[Florida]], USA]]

Origin uncertain; the following etymologies have been suggested:

* The first edition of the ''{{w|International Cloud Atlas}} (1896),<ref>{{cite-book|author=International Meterological Committee|authorlink=International Meteorological Organization|author2=H[ugo Hildebrand] Hildebrandsson|authorlink2=Hugo Hildebrand Hildebrandsson|author3=A[lbert] Riggenbach|authorlink3=Albert Riggenbach|author4=L[éon] Teisserenc de Bort|authorlink4=Léon Teisserenc de Bort|title=[[w:International Cloud Atlas|Atlas international des nuages = International Cloud-atlas = Internationaler Wolken-Atlas]]|location=Paris|publisher=Gauthier-Villars|year=1896|oclc=715068869}}.</ref> which defined ten types of cloud, described the ninth type as the [[cumulonimbus]] which rises to 10 km (6.2 miles), the highest a cloud can be.<ref name="Etymonline">{{R:Online Etymology Dictionary|url=https://www.etymonline.com/word/cloud%20nine|accessdate=22 December 2017}}</ref>
* In traditional [[Han Chinese]] mythology the sky has nine layers. The ninth cloud ({{m|cnm|九霄|tr=jiǔxiāo}}: {{m|cnm|九|tr=jiǔ||nine}} + {{m|cnm|霄|tr=xiāo||sky; clouds, mist; night}}) is the highest part of the sky or, in [[Taoism]], [[heaven]] where the gods live.

Compare {{m|en|cloud seven||state of complete happiness or euphoria}},<ref>{{cite-book|author=Harold Wentworth and {{w|Stuart Berg Flexner}}, compilers and editors|title=Dictionary of American Slang|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=Thomas T. Crowell|year=1960|oclc=803362919}}.</ref> which may have originated from confusion of ''cloud nine'' with {{m|en|seventh heaven}}.<ref name="Etymonline"/>

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP|GA}} {{IPA|/ˈklaʊd ˈnaɪn/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} ''Often in the phrase'' '''{{l|en|on cloud nine}}''': a [[state#Noun|state]] of [[bliss]], [[elation]] or [[happiness]].
#: {{ux|en|He was on '''cloud nine''' for days after she agreed to marry him.}}

